Z||000002||Oreif||01-03-2001||02:31 AM||||Here is the original album cover and the posting for the band. They only had 2 albums.<BR>You would need to find a place where you can locate import albums. They were only sold in Germany, Greece, Spain, and the UK. <BR>(I already checked with CD-NOW and they don't have it)<P>BTW ~ for their other album and the 2 "Singles" they put out. Go to:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.home.zonnet.nl/snamyook/rl/covers.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.home.zonnet.nl/snamyook/rl/covers.html</A> <P>And scroll down to the "O's". (This link also lists EVERY band that has ever sang/played "Radar Love" It is one long list! AND the original band who wrote it "Golden Earring" isn't on the list!)<P><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/OHW.jpg">    <P>Oh Well - 1st Album <BR> <BR>Tracks:<BR>Hit You, Mad day in London, <B>Radar Love,</B> Don't waste my Time, Day by Day, Oh Well, Stop the World, I'll be forever your Man, Downtown, We will Rock you, I'll be forever your man (Mix)<P>Great dance-version of Radar Love <BR>    <BR>Countries: Germany, Greece, Spain, UK <BR>Year: 1990<BR>LP: 88-Records/EMI 793447 1 <BR>CD: 88-Records/EMI 793447 2 <BR>LP: Parlophone/EMI 7340 1 (UK)<BR>CD: Parlophone/EMI 7340 2 (UK)<P> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-03-2001).]||||reg||1
